Subject: port: link loadable modules into the server on WASIX
Last-Update: 2026-09-29

WASIX has no dynamic loader. Build each loadable module as a static
archive for the server to link in, compiling the two entry points the
fmgr interface names under a per-module prefix so that modules do not
collide, and give dfmgr.c a table of them, generated by the build:
dlopen() returns a module's table entry and dlsym() searches its entry
points. A linked-in module has no file, so the scan of loaded modules
by name is its whole identity check. Installing a module installs its
archive where its shared object would have gone.

